# Settings > Updates > Packages (report 047 P4, the owner's "is it frozen?" requirement): every long wait shows it is alive.
# A slow board (apt slow on: the reassurance line at once), the deck case (tests/fixtures/apt/deck-p4). The first scan:
# the working box (title, the step in plain words, the bar at stage n of 4, the elapsed counter mm:ss, "This board is
# slow..."); held at stage 1 (reading the package lists), then at stage 2 (finding the packages that can be upgraded) at
# 00:23; 20 s after the last step change the second line ("Still working..."); the list then shows while the plan's
# closure runs (stage 4: a small inline status with its elapsed counter, the Upgrade row "checking"); Upgrade pressed
# before the plan is ready: the box "Preparing the upgrade" until it is, then the confirmation (21 packages). Upgrade now:
# "Starting the helper..." with its elapsed counter and the moving bar until the helper's first status; the helper's
# check phase: "Checking the plan  00:17" and the reassurance row. Every label whole (expect_unclipped). Keys only.
# Review only: no golden.
title updates wait
review
sizes 640x480 480x800 480x640 720x720 1280x800 480x320
@480x800,480x640 profile pda
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env HARNESS_APPS missing
env HARNESS_SUDO ok
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30 2026-11-01
wifi 70
bt on
update net on
update build 0.9.2 release arm64
update answer releases-real.json
apt slow on
apt board pending
apt lists-age 1
home
launch Settings
wait 300
key UP
key UP
key UP
key UP
key ENTER
wait 1000
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 8000
# 1. stage 1 of 4: reading the package lists (the board's apt-get -s takes long)
shot wait_scan_reading
expect_text "Preparing the updates"
expect_text "Esc cancels"
expect_unclipped "Preparing the updates" "Reading the package lists" "This board is slow: it can take a minute. Nothing is frozen."
# 2. stage 2 of 4 at 00:23: finding the packages that can be upgraded
apt hold listing
apt board deck-p4
wait 10700
shot wait_scan_stage2
expect_unclipped "Preparing the updates" "Finding the packages that can be upgraded" "00:23" "Esc cancels"
# 3. 20 s with no step change: the second line
wait 11000
shot wait_scan_still
expect_unclipped "Still working... the packages list is long" "This board is slow: it can take a minute. Nothing is frozen."
# 4. the list is out, the plan's closure runs (held): an inline status, the Upgrade row "checking"
apt hold checking
wait 1500
shot wait_plan_inline
expect_text "checking"
expect_text "Refresh lists"
# the highlight on the first row (the list replaced the box: not the last row)
expect_unclipped "Refresh lists" "Upgrade packages"
# 5. Upgrade pressed before the plan is ready: the box until it is
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 600
shot wait_plan_box
expect_text "Preparing the upgrade"
expect_unclipped "Preparing the upgrade" "Checking that the upgrade is safe"
# 6. the plan is ready: on to the confirmation (the closure: 21 packages)
apt hold none
wait 2000
shot wait_plan_done
expect_text "Upgrade now"
expect_text "Launcher libraries (6)"
# 7. Upgrade now: the helper's unit started, no status yet: "Starting the helper..." and the moving bar
key END
key UP
key ENTER
wait 3000
shot wait_helper_start
expect_text start "Starting the helper..."
expect_text "Check the plan"
expect_unclipped "Check the plan" "Download" "Install" "Clean up" "Slow board: nothing is frozen"
# 8. the helper's check phase at 17 s: its elapsed counter, the reassurance row, Cancel
apt upgrade job upgrade
apt upgrade state running
apt upgrade phase check
apt upgrade total 21
apt upgrade started now-17
apt upgrade log /var/log/cyberdeckzero/apt-upgrade-20261101-203000.log
wait 1500
expect_text "Checking the plan  00:17"
shot wait_check_phase
expect_text "Cancel"
expect_text "Slow board: nothing is frozen"
expect_unclipped "Check the plan" "Download" "Install" "Clean up" "Cancel" "Slow board: nothing is frozen"
apt upgrade state cancelled
apt upgrade reason cancelled while checking: nothing was installed
wait 1500
key ESC
key ESC
key ESC
wait 300
